# Module — ignore / do not customize `classes/seller_partner/`

`classes/seller_partner/` is a **build-time vendored copy** of
`shopify-amazon-spapi-connector`, not module-owned business logic.

## How the overwrite works

Amazon package builds enable `BUILD_INTEGRATE_SELLER_PARTNER=1`:

| Profile script | Source folder | Package dir |
|---|---|---|
| `../build_amazon_saas_module.sh` | `Prestashop-SAAS-Module` | `amazonsaas` |
| `../build_amazon_module.sh` | `Prestashop-Amazon` | `amazon` |

Both call `../build_module.sh` -> `integrate_seller_partner()`:

1. Resolve connector path (`SHOPIFY_SPAPI_PATH` or `SHOPIFY_SPAPI_CANDIDATES`).
2. **`rm -rf ./classes/seller_partner`** inside the build package directory.
3. **`rsync`** the entire connector tree into `./classes/seller_partner/`.

That runs **after** the module source is copied into the package. Any local edits under `classes/seller_partner/` are wiped from the ZIP and **never ship**.

Legacy Amazon also lists `/classes/seller_partner/` in `.gitignore` (working tree only). SaaS may keep a local copy for development; the ZIP still replaces it on every Amazon build.

## Do not

- Edit, refactor, or "fix" product/feed/listing business logic under
  `classes/seller_partner/` (including `feeds/`, `feeds/json/`, `catalog/`, ...).
- Put PrestaShop-module-only behaviour (WINE `item_volume`, profile rules,
  marketplace-specific feed tweaks, etc.) in connector classes.
- Rely on changes under `seller_partner/` surviving `build_amazon_saas_module.sh`
  or `build_amazon_module.sh`.

## Where module-specific logic belongs

| Need | Put it in |
|---|---|
| JSON listing attributes before send | `classes/AmazonJsonFeedsSending.php` |
| Catalog export / profile field assembly | `functions/products_json.php`, `functions/profiles_json.php`, `functions/json_operations.php` |
| Shared WINE volume helpers (SaaS) | `classes/amazon.wine.volume.class.php` |
| Module-owned SP feed helpers that must ship | `classes/` outside `seller_partner/` (e.g. legacy `AmazonSPFeedJsonMessageFulfillmentChannelSwitch`) |
| Connector / SP-API client bugs | Fix in `shopify-amazon-spapi-connector`, then rebuild the module ZIP |

## If `seller_partner/` appears modified for a module ticket

- Prefer reverting those files unless the change is a deliberate connector sync.
- Re-implement the behaviour in module-owned paths above.
- Do not treat `seller_partner/` hits as first-party scope in reviews or codemods.

## Match adapters to the shipped connector tree

Module adapters outside `seller_partner/` (e.g. `AmazonLogger`, quota / endpoint
handlers) must resolve interfaces and classes **as they exist under
`classes/seller_partner/` after connector sync** — not from a stale local copy
that may still carry a different `namespace`.

- Connector / SP-API bugs: fix in `shopify-amazon-spapi-connector`, then rebuild
  the module ZIP.
- Do **not** "paper over" a mismatch by adding or changing `namespace` only in
  the SaaS/local `classes/seller_partner/` tree — that copy is wiped on build and
  never ships.
